fact WorkItem(id: "WI-725", description: some(value: "The [simp] type-directed firing guard (simp_guard_holds_core in kb/typing.rs, shared by the typer simp_fire_guard_holds and the resolver simp_requires_guard_holds) refuses to fire a <=>/= [simp] rewrite whose spec-op carrier is typed at the SPEC SORT ITSELF — a constructor-less abstract sort used DIRECTLY as its own carrier. VERIFIED failure (WI-714 where increment, empirically bisected with instrumentation): where(r: Relation, cond) is a member of the abstract sort Relation, so lookup_spec_op_dispatch(where) = Relation and the guard classifies it as a spec op; the guard then requires every carrier argument sort to sort_provides the spec sort Relation. The carrier person_row : Relation has sort head Relation, and sort_provides(Relation, Relation) = false (a sort does not provide itself — Relation provides LogicalStream, not Relation). So the guard returns DontFire, try_fire returns None, the where <=> guarded_of [simp] rewrite NEVER fires, and the body-less where op reaches eval as UnknownOperation. ASYMMETRY: the other self-representing containers (Set/Map/List/Stream) have CONCRETE carriers that PROVIDE the abstract spec so the guard passes; Relation is the first spec sort used DIRECTLY as its own carrier (a rule-reference relation value is typed Relation[schema]), so its carrier sort IS the spec sort. FIX DIRECTION: in the self-representing branch of simp_guard_holds_core (typing.rs ~25494, the Some(carrier) if sort_provides(...) arm), also accept self_representing && same_sort_canonical(carrier, spec_sort) — a value typed at the abstract sort directly IS a valid carrier for a law declared on that sort. Empirically verified: with this one-line change the guard fires and the WI-714 where macro (guarded_of) runs to its next stage. Sound: a value whose static sort IS the spec sort trivially carries the spec. Blast radius = the shared guard (typer + resolver), so verify BOTH phases. ACCEPTANCE: cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh; a minimal <=> [simp] rule whose LHS is a member operation of a constructor-less abstract sort, invoked on a value typed directly at that sort, fires the rewrite (regression test); the existing spec-op-law guard behavior is unchanged (a concrete carrier whose sort does NOT provide the spec still DontFires). Blocks WI-714 where/join (proposal 052); surfaced empirically by the where increment. Rust-only (typer + resolver simp guard)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-16T05:56:18Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-725", author: "claude", content: "CORRECTED FIX (the ticket FIX DIRECTION was WRONG, verified empirically). The proposed reflexive-guard change (accept same_sort_canonical(carrier, spec_sort) in simp_guard_holds_core) IS too broad: it fires EVERY self-representing spec law on an abstract carrier, so a value-RHS reducing law get(put(m,k,v),k) <=> some(v) rewrites a Map op body to some(1) which breaks at eval (UnknownOperation some) — the exact WI-611 catch-22 the WI-596 authors deliberately avoided (refine-to-provider, NOT reflexive-fire). With the reflexive fix the full suite went 2 red (map_builtins proposal_acceptance_fixture + wi724 single-column). ACTUAL FIX = distinguish a definitional LOWERING from a conditional typeclass LAW by the RHS: a [simp] rule whose RHS head is a MACRO (is_macro; occurrence->occurrence; e.g. where <=> guarded_of) is a compile-time syntax->syntax lowering — the macro is its own validity check — so it BYPASSES the spec-op carrier guard; a value-RHS law stays gated (WI-611 preserved). LOCUS = kb/simp_rewrite.rs try_fire: new stored_rhs_functor(rid) (sibling of stored_lhs_functor; reads the stored equation RHS head at pos_args[1], no DeBruijn open) + is_macro, checked ONLY when the carrier guard failed (guard_ok/guard_failed memoized; guard stays BEFORE open_equation, WI-655 cost model kept). Sound: the guard is side-effect-free; a macro reads matched occurrences and can decline (return non-Node -> template kept -> loud downstream error). simp_guard_holds_core itself is UNCHANGED (reverted). Test wi725_self_carried_spec_simp_test.rs: a macro-RHS lowering on a constructor-less abstract self-carrier (Widget; sort_provides(Widget,Widget) false) fires (use_flip body rewrites flip(w) -> macro output noted(w)); counterfactual-verified (bypass off -> flip stays dormant -> MissingRequires load error). The value-RHS dual (a Map reducing law still does NOT fire on an abstract carrier) is pinned by map_builtins_test::proposal_acceptance_fixture. Full workspace suite 2885/0. [[verify-before-declaring-blocker]]", at: "2026-07-16T05:35:03Z")
